adding a screen destination does not always show the destiantion straight away and need a manual refresh button action.
  >> DONE 1c5d035. Same 5-second cache as the project-load item, and your report is
     what confirmed it. After adding a destination the code called a plain ctx.load(),
     which is served from the client payload cache - so on a hit it re-rendered a
     snapshot taken BEFORE the destination existed and the new row was just missing.
     The Refresh button always worked because it forces a refetch. "Not always" is
     precisely the cache window: it only misses if a snapshot was fetched in the
     preceding 5 seconds, which is why it felt random.
     Fixed the reported site plus the three others in that file with the same shape
     (host-channel add, device-snapshot applied, caspar-config applied). Guard now
     fails if any bare ctx.load() reappears in device-view-events.js.
     Worth noting: I had these exact lines fixed an hour ago and reverted them because
     I could not justify the scope at the time. You just justified them.
     NEEDS KIOSK RELOAD.


